  "prefLabel": "Lot 7202.11 Electronic table game (ETG)",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Lot 7202.11 “Electronic table game (ETG)” means a VLT comprised of a combination of a player interface and all interface elements that function collectively for the purpose of electronically simulating live table game operations including but not limited to the automated collection of bets and payout winnings. ETGs may be played with or without the assistance of a live dealer or as a hybrid system.\n\nSource. #14341, EMERGENCY, eff 8-21-25; ss by #14503, eff 2-4-26, EXPIRES: 2-4-36 (formerly Lot 7202.07)",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/lot7200.html"
